    rationale:
      "Confirmed as a real, previously-unaudited, non-self-healing visibility gap in the class AGENT_PROTOCOL already treats as first-class (see commerce-buy-now-client-receipt-visibility, stripe-connect-onboarding-pipeline-health-visibility): a signal already computable from already-shipped data with zero operator-facing surface. Scoped this iteration to visibility only (aggregate count + staleness age + a row-level read-only panel), matching the two-PR precedent commerce-buy-now-client-receipt-visibility itself set (visibility first, manual resend as a distinct follow-up) — a bundle resend action needs the DNS-handoff email body, which is currently built inline in the webhook route rather than as a reusable helper the way sendReceiptEmail already is for the receipt half; extracting that safely is left as a scoped follow-up rather than risking a webhook regression in the same change.\n\nShipped: isBundleHandoffMissingBuyerEmail (src/lib/payments/bundle-side-effect-recovery.ts) — a pure predicate, true when a handoff has a non-blank customerEmail but is missing the receipt and/or DNS sent-marker note (mirrors planBundleWebhookSideEffects's own hasCustomerEmail gate so a handoff with no email on file, which never attempts either send, never reports as 'missing'). computePipelineHealth (src/lib/metrics/pipeline-health.ts) now derives bundleOrdersMissingBuyerEmailCount / oldestBundleOrdersMissingBuyerEmailAgeHours directly from its existing required `handoffs` input (no new optional param, no new DB round trip — every call site already passes listDeployHandoffs()), reusing the existing oldestOpenHandoffAgeHours helper for the staleness signal. PipelineHealthPanel gained a matching 'Bundle buyer email missing' MetricCard, placed beside the existing bundle refund/dispute cards. buildDailyDigest (src/lib/digest/daily-digest.ts) computes the same set from its existing optional `handoffs` input (already wired at every call site for the open-handoffs section) and adds a capped 'Bundle buyer email missing' email section (5-row display cap, uncapped *Count per the AGENT_PROTOCOL debt-list rule) with per-row missingReceipt/missingDnsHandoff flags so the digest names exactly which email is still outstanding, not just 'something is missing'; folded the new count into the single-source-of-truth actionableSections array (not a hand-duplicated isEmpty check) per the daily-digest-empty-state-copy-drift precedent. leads-client.tsx gained a read-only 'Bundle buyer email missing' due-queue panel (no action button, matching the precedent set by the genuinely-read-only Bundle order refunds & disputes panel one section above it — the buyer's email is the natural remediation channel here, not an internal db field), computing bundleHandoffsMissingBuyerEmail client-side from the handoffs state array already passed down as initialHandoffs, with the standard heading id + tabIndex={-1} + aria-live=\"polite\" aria-relevant=\"removals\" markup every sibling due-queue panel already uses.\n\nAdded 6 new unit cases for isBundleHandoffMissingBuyerEmail to bundle-side-effect-recovery.test.ts, a new pipeline-health.test.ts case covering all four handoff shapes (missing both/missing DNS only/fully notified/no customer email) in one assertion, and a new daily-digest.test.ts case asserting the sorted row order, per-row missingReceipt/missingDnsHandoff flags, and the true uncapped count — plus updated the existing actionableSectionLabels regression-list test for the new section label. Verified: npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json (0 errors) + npm run lint (clean) + npx vitest run (2945 passed, +12 over the pre-iteration 2933 post-archive-split baseline, 204 files) + a full clean rebuild (rm -rf .next && npm run build, clean, same 42-route ○/ƒ split) + npm run dev smoke check (/dashboard/leads and / both 200; confirmed the new 'Bundle buyer email missing' MetricCard renders with its zero-state copy against seeded demo data with no matching handoffs, and that the row-level panel correctly stays unmounted at zero rather than rendering an empty section; dev server killed, port freed). NEXT_STEPS unchanged — all five gated items remain operator/legal/infra-blocked; this closes a real sold-capability-wiring visibility gap on an already-shipped, already-redelivery-safe bundle email path, not any of the five gated items. Diff-gate anchor moves to ca19f7be (this session's own starting tip, post-PR-#764).",
