      "Unattended scheduled routine (\"continue toward a profitable and growing business, merge changes when done\"), branch claude/nice-euler-w89qe4. Session started at origin/main tip ca19f7be — same as bundle-order-missing-buyer-email-visibility's own starting point — but that PR (#765) was still open (not yet merged) when this session began; merged it first (no live fold candidate otherwise, and it was a complete, already-tested, already-mergeable sibling PR sitting on the exact current main tip) rather than duplicating its work, then rebased onto the resulting main tip (934ed1e7) before starting fresh work. Confirmed baseline green from that fresh tip: npm ci (409 packages, 9 known high-severity findings, unchanged, dev-only) + npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json (0 errors) + npm run lint (clean). A `git fetch origin '+refs/heads/*:refs/remotes/origin/*' --prune` sweep of the newest ~20 remote branches by push time found each either byte-identical to an already-merged PR or fully superseded — no further live fold candidate.\n\nDispatched a research agent explicitly steered at PR #765's own body, which named its deliberately-deferred follow-up: 'manual resend needs the DNS email body extracted out of the webhook route into a reusable helper first.' It confirmed the follow-up was still open: src/app/api/stripe/webhook/route.ts still built the bundle DNS/go-live handoff email inline (subject + HTML wrapper around formatDnsInstructionsForEmail, then a raw sendEmail(...) call) with no standalone `sendBundleDnsHandoffEmail`-style export in src/lib/email/resend.ts the way sendReceiptEmail already exists for the receipt half, and the 'Bundle buyer email missing' dashboard panel PR #765 shipped had zero action button — just static copy telling the operator to reply to the customer directly. This session independently re-verified both claims by reading the webhook route and leads-client.tsx panel directly before implementing.",
    rationale:
      "Closing this follow-up completes the two-PR precedent commerce-buy-now-client-receipt-visibility itself set (visibility first, manual resend second) for the bundle ledger the same way it was already closed for Commerce Buy now — a permanently-bad buyer email or a sustained Resend outage past Stripe's finite webhook-retry window previously left the operator with visibility but no in-app remediation; they had to manually reconstruct the DNS instructions and compose an email outside the app.\n\nShipped: sendBundleDnsHandoffEmail (src/lib/email/resend.ts) — extracted the exact HTML/subject the webhook route built inline into a standalone export (same skipSuppression: true billing-critical class as sendReceiptEmail), imported from src/lib/deploy/dns-email.ts (the pure formatDnsInstructionsForEmail module, not src/lib/deploy/handoff.ts, to avoid pulling that module's db-touching surface into resend.ts's import graph beyond what it already needed). Swapped the webhook route's inline construction for a call to this new helper — one template now backs both the automatic webhook send and the new manual resend, closing the drift risk a duplicated copy would have created. resendBundleBuyerEmailAction (src/app/dashboard/leads/actions.ts) — the row-level remedy for isBundleHandoffMissingBuyerEmail, mirroring resendCommerceClientReceiptAction's shape (requireOperatorAuth → checkRateLimit(bundle-buyer-email-resend:<ip>) → parseLeadSlugLookup → fetch-before-write). Takes a leadSlug (not a stripeSessionId) since a bundle deploy handoff is one row per lead (getDeployHandoffBySlug), not one row per Checkout Session the way a Commerce Buy now order is. Checks hasBundleReceiptEmailNote/hasBundleDnsHandoffEmailNote directly and sends only whichever half is still missing — a handoff where the receipt already sent but DNS failed only gets the DNS email re-sent, never a duplicate receipt. Writes a durable sent-marker note only for whichever half's send actually resolved `{ success: true }` (never on throw or `{ success: false }`, matching the marker-write invariant this file's AGENT_PROTOCOL entry already states for the webhook's own emails) via updateDeployHandoffStatus + DEPLOY_HANDOFF_CONVEX_PRIMARY (fail-closed on ConvexPrimaryWriteError, same policy Mark live / Assign Vercel project / Assign custom domain already use for this table) — a single updateDeployHandoffStatus call appends both markers together when both sends succeed, so a fully-resolved handoff only takes one write. A partial failure (one half sends, the other doesn't) still durably marks the succeeded half and returns success:false with a message naming which one to retry, rather than either losing the successful send's marker or silently reporting overall success. The dashboard panel gained a per-row 'Resend {missing half(s)}' button (mirroring the Commerce 'Resend receipt' button's styling/pattern) that updates the leads-client.tsx `handoffs` state array from the action's returned handoff so the derived bundleHandoffsMissingBuyerEmail list recomputes correctly whether the resend fully or only partially resolved; focus only moves to the panel heading when the row actually unmounts (fully resolved), never when a partial success leaves the button in place — same a11y invariant as the read-only panel's sibling due-queues, extended to handle the new non-binary (partial) outcome this feature introduces that no prior resend action in this codebase had to handle.\n\nUpdated src/app/api/stripe/webhook/route.test.ts's `@/lib/email/resend` mock and every DNS-handoff-path assertion to reference the new sendBundleDnsHandoffEmail export instead of the generic sendEmail (which the DNS handler no longer calls directly) — including retargeting the 'unexpected DNS email formatting fails' case, which previously exercised a real formatDnsInstructionsForEmail throw on a malformed `dnsInstructions: null` handoff; since that formatting now runs inside the (fully mocked, in this suite) sendBundleDnsHandoffEmail export rather than inline in route.ts, the equivalent coverage is now sendBundleDnsHandoffEmail.mockRejectedValue(...) — an unexpected send/formatting failure still returns 500 (bundle_email_send) without losing the receipt marker already written, same observable contract, without depending on an internal implementation detail of a function this test file no longer exercises for real. Added 3 new resend.test.ts cases (businessName escaping + DNS-instructions inclusion, brand.name escaping, still-delivers-when-suppressed) and a new resend-bundle-buyer-email-action.test.ts (15 cases: auth, rate-limit, empty/over-long slug, handoff not-found, no-buyer-email, both-already-sent guard, full success writing both markers in one call, missing-half-only send, $0 amount fallback when no bundle order row is found, partial-failure marker-preservation, all-sends-failed no-marker-write, ConvexPrimaryWriteError fail-closed, null-handoff-after-write, unexpected marker-persist error).\n\nVerified: npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json (0 errors) + npm run lint (clean) + npx vitest run (2963 passed, +18 over the pre-iteration 2945 post-PR-#765 baseline, 205 files) + a full clean rebuild (rm -rf .next && npm run build, clean, same 42-route ○/ƒ split) + npm run dev smoke check (/dashboard/leads and /docs/architecture both 200; confirmed 'Bundle buyer email missing' and 'resendBundleBuyerEmailAction' text render in the served HTML; dev server killed, port 3100 confirmed freed, local.db deleted afterward). NEXT_STEPS unchanged — all five gated items remain operator/legal/infra-blocked; this closes the deliberately-deferred manual-resend follow-up from bundle-order-missing-buyer-email-visibility, not any of the five gated items. Diff-gate anchor moves to 934ed1e7 (this session's own starting tip after merging PR #765).",
